  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nA novel approach using a factorization into sine and cosine components allows representation of correlated step functions in a transformed optimization space. By leveraging the intersection of Fourier analysis and optimization, we parameterize the function as a linear combination of sine and cosine bases. This formulation preserves the non-negativity and integral constraints while producing smoother gradients suitable for optimization. The method effectively handles the complex shift-optimization by projecting into a space where correlation penalties are naturally separable.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\nLet h(x) = U^T a(x) where U is orthogonal matrix of Fourier coefficients. Parameters a satisfy:\n- 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 (handled implicitly via Fourier clipping)\n- \u222bh(x)dx=1 (enforced via projection)\n- Minimize max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\nThe optimization formulates a penalized least-squares problem with adaptive projection. Gradients are computed via matrix multiplications (O(n) per parameter) providing significant speed improvements over finite differences.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nValidate parent input and determine approximation order (orders 8-12). Initialize coefficients via Slepian sequence projection. Implement block-optimization with iterative:\n- Fourier basis projection\n- Augmented Lagrangian updates (constraint handling)\n- Schur-complement based gradient descent\nUse trust-region methods and spectral step control. Quadratic-time operations are minimized by factor caching and low-rank approximations.\n\n4. Search Choices/Useful Variations:\nInclude warm starts with four different orders (8,10,12,14) and three different basis sets (Fourier, Chebyshev, Legendre) per phase. Maintain stability with polynomial filtering, currently using:\n- Initial filter coefficient: 0.7\n- Filter window: 5 steps\n- Step control: 0.95 relaxed updates\n\n5. Compute Budget & Robustness:\nAllocate 100 steps for order 8, 300 for order 10, and 800 for order 12 operations. Monitor progress at 40% and 80% completion. Reproduce total time as T_total \u2248 6n/CPUs minutes. Fallback to basic block optimization on failure.\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\nProgram ensures:\n- Integral constraint: \u222bh(x)dx=1 with error |\u222bh dx - 1| \u2264 1e-4\n- Boundary: 0\u2264h(x)\u22641 with |hmax - 1| \u2264 0.01 and |hmin| \u2248 0\n- Overlap score accuracy: |target_c - computed_c| \u2264 1e-3\nImplementation includes:\n- Fast quadratic forms via factor caching\n- Analytical gradient calculation\n- Strict projection enforcement\n- Performance monitoring checkpoints",
